Reference
.........
schema:spatialCoverage

Definition
..........
The spatialCoverage of a CreativeWork indicates the place(s) which are the focus of the content. It is a subproperty of
      contentLocation intended primarily for more technical and detailed materials. For example with a Dataset, it indicates
      areas that the dataset describes: a dataset of New York weather would have spatialCoverage which was the place: the state of New York.

Scope
.....
Domain: CreativeWork (https://schema.org/CreativeWork).
Range: Place (https://schema.org/Place).


CDIF
----

Definition
..........
Geographic extent of resource content.

Scope
.....
schema:spatialCoverage - geographic extent of the dataset's content.
</body>
                  </ownedComment>
                  <lowerValue xmi:id="CoreDiscovery.Dataset-spatialCoverage-lowerValue" xmi:uuid="https://w3id.org/cdif/discovery/1.1/composite/xmi/#Dataset-spatialCoverage-lowerValue" xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger">
                     <value>0</value>
                  </lowerValue>
                  <upperValue xmi:id="CoreDiscovery.Dataset-spatialCoverage-upperValue" xmi:uuid="https://w3id.org/cdif/discovery/1.1/composite/xmi/#Dataset-spatialCoverage-upperValue" xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural">
                     <value>*</value>
                  </upperValue>
                  <name>spatialCoverage</name>
                  <type xmi:idref="CoreDiscovery.SpatialExtent"/>
